      "contentType": "text/html; charset=utf-8",
      "textPreview": "Backyard Breaks x ClipHouse Master Clipper SOP What to clip, how to edit it, how to caption it, and how to submit. The Campaign in One Sentence Make cold US viewers understand the money fast. Price stops the scroll, reaction earns the watch time, rarity drives comments. 1. The Most Important Rules &#8252;&#65039; &bull; Target the US audience. Backyard Breaks sells through live streams, so the content needs to reach people likely to watch and buy in the United States. &bull; NO commenting/responding to user comments on posts. &bull; Show the card price clearly on screen. Do not make viewers guess why the pull matters. PRICE MUST BE CORRECT. &bull; Use the tracker value exactly. If the tracker gives a range, use the range or safe wording like \"$100K+\". &bull; Open fast. The first 3 seconds should show money, rarity, reaction, or tension. &bull; Use the campaign hashtag stack: #BackyardBreaks #BBPulls #Whatnot 2. What Clips Do Best Priority Clip Type What To Look For 1 Huge card value $10K+, $50K+, $100K+, six figures, seven figures. Price is the scroll-stopper. 2 1/1 rarity Logoman, Papa / Padparadscha, Superfractor, Gold Vinyl, Shield. One copy in the world is easy to understand. 3"
